    <h1>Chronotecture
      <span class="sub">The Giza Course Countdown — 204 levels of bricks, 1902 to 2106&nbsp;AD</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="prov">A rebuild of Jason&nbsp;M.&nbsp;Breshears’ hand-drawn chart&nbsp;I·e (Breshears&nbsp;’07), with every date, span and annotation preserved verbatim; only the visual language is new. Its structural key: <b>1902&nbsp;AD [5796&nbsp;AM], where the Stonehenge chronolithic system ends</b>. Seven bars run forward from it, from 144&nbsp;months to 144&nbsp;years, and the countdown of <b>204 levels of bricks [years], 2448&nbsp;months</b>, ends at 6000&nbsp;Annus&nbsp;Mundi [2106&nbsp;AD].</p>
  </header>

